Carrier ledger:
- edge_tail_tip_recursive_witness [two_ended_tournament_packet] score=9
  preserves: the overlap predicate as a two-ended witness with both marginal deletion children
  destroys/audits: exact time coordinate and high Fourier phase unless cross-sector or analytic sidecar is retained
  next_test: add edge_witness_id, tail_child, tip_child, and cross_sector_orientation_word to few-apex rows
- l2_cauchy_schwarz_tail_floor [existing_spectral_floor] score=8
  preserves: a rigorous-style low-frequency exact sum plus Parseval tail bound for Rprime
  destroys/audits: local endpoint ownership and the reason a bad frequency appears
  next_test: turn lrc14_spectrum_L2tail_synthesis_kpswf12 into a finite HYP-3121 row certificate
- cross_sector_orientation_word [observer_cut_sidecar] score=7
  preserves: the first concrete orientation coordinate that repairs edge-sector quotient collapse
  destroys/audits: the analytic size of the overlap if used without measure or Fourier data
  next_test: test whether any multi-far packet collision survives sector counts plus orientation
- gaussian_heat_kernel_smoothing [smooth_correlation_floor] score=6
  preserves: a smoothed positive correlation floor with exponentially damped Fourier tails
  destroys/audits: sharp boundary atoms unless a finite-ruler desmoothing margin is retained
  next_test: prove smoothed Rprime_t >= c_t and desmooth through finite denominator thresholds
- endpoint_phi_activation_gate [exact_gap_circuit_gate] score=5
  preserves: the exact endpoint-cover gap sum and max activation from HYP-2108/HYP-2112
  destroys/audits: distribution across residue channels if endpoint activations are scalarized
  next_test: join Phi_gap, P_max_activation, and edge_witness_id in one packet schema
- normal_fan_cech_finite_ruler [component_topology_floor] score=4
  preserves: normalized component and finite-ruler payload for the few-apex floor
  destroys/audits: tail/tip covariance and Fourier phases if topology is isolated
  next_test: combine Cech beta, owner currents, and Gaussian/L2 floor certificates
- asano_endpoint_contraction [multiaffine_zero_free_contraction] score=3
  preserves: endpoint/tail-tip interaction variables while preserving a zero-free sector under contraction
  destroys/audits: metric size of the safe arcs unless coefficients are tied back to Phi/P activation
  next_test: build a two-end partition polynomial and check whether contraction preserves nonvanishing
- elliott_halberstam_level_packet [average_distribution_schema] score=2
  preserves: average residue-channel discrepancy control, analogous to level of distribution one
  destroys/audits: worst individual residue/channel behavior and exact witness time
  next_test: define finite channel errors over q, residue, edge-witness, and Fourier shells; prove an averaged bound
- raw_bonferroni_scalar [negative_control] score=1
  preserves: only the measure-sum obstruction that already fails on few-apex examples
  destroys/audits: all correlation structure; it cannot see Rprime when mu(A)+mu(B)<1
  next_test: keep only as a failure alarm, never as a closure route
- raw_edge_count_shadow [negative_control] score=0
  preserves: small tournament size telemetry
  destroys/audits: tail/tip role, sector orientation, deletion recursion, and LRC predicate
  next_test: use only to sanity-check finite enumeration

6. HYP-3125 HANDOFF ROUTES FOR THE UNIFORM Rprime >= c FLOOR
A. Edge-witness route: encode R-safe and Q-lonely as the two ends of a witness edge.  Tail and tip deletion children are the marginals; the cross-sector word is the covariance payload.  A collapse to empty intersection is legal only if a child or cross-sector coordinate names the debt.
B. Elliott-Halberstam-style route: do not ask for every residue/fiber to be uniform.  Ask for a level-of-distribution average over channels (q, residue, edge_witness_id, Fourier shell).  This is an analogy, not a prime theorem import: the target is a finite discrepancy inequality whose averaged error is below the product mass.
C. Gaussian route: heat-smooth the two indicator events, prove a smoothed positive correlation using damped Fourier tails, then desmooth through a finite-ruler margin.  This is the analytic sibling of the existing L2-Cauchy-Schwarz tail certificate.
D. Asano route: make endpoint/tail-tip interactions multiaffine, then contract the two endpoint variables while preserving a zero-free sector. If the contracted polynomial remains nonvanishing in the legal sector and coefficients still read back to Phi/P activation, empty overlap is forbidden or routed to named debt.

Assumption challenge:
Chosen vertices here are edge witnesses, residue/Fourier channels, and proof carriers.  The preserved predicate for the handoff is the LRC14 covering witness R-safe intersect Q-lonely nonempty, equivalently a positive Rprime floor in HYP-3125.  The quotient destroys exact time, endpoint owner, phase, and sometimes tail/tip role.  Those coordinates must be retained, averaged with a finite error budget, resurrected by Gaussian/Asano/endpoint sidecars, or emitted as named HYP-2968/HYP-3121 debt before the HYP-3125 edge_floor_packet compresses them.
